% A !fermata!, !trill! or !breath! just before a bar line decorates the
% bar line, which abc2midi does not play.  It was kept for the first note
% after the bar line, which was lengthened, trilled or shortened.  The
% notes below are all played plain, with the beat stress of their place.
% Tune 2 puts shorthand decorations, such as H for !fermata!, before bar
% lines of several kinds, as section 4.14 of the abc standard allows
% (GitHub issue #57).  parsenote() (parseabc.c) required a note after
% them, so that they were a "Malformed note".
X:1
T:Decorations on bar lines
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/4
Q:1/4=120
K:C
C D E F !fermata!|G A B c !trill!|c B A G !breath!|F E D C |]

X:2
T:Shorthand decorations on bar lines
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/4
Q:1/4=120
K:C
|:C D E F H|G A B c T :|c B A G S||F E D C ~[|E D C2 H|]
